1
00:01:28,912 --> 00:01:34,751
MALE BONDING IN A CYPRESS BATHTUB

2
00:01:40,157 --> 00:01:41,158
So cool!

3
00:01:41,592 --> 00:01:43,694
It's the BUGATTI Ryotsu Special.

4
00:01:44,461 --> 00:01:47,164
It's not just fast. Watch this.

5
00:01:47,898 --> 00:01:48,899
-Terai! -Huh?

6
00:01:51,535 --> 00:01:53,737
Unmatched cornering performance.

7
00:01:53,937 --> 00:01:54,938
That's amazing!

8
00:01:56,440 --> 00:02:01,144
It's got disc brakes, it's got lights, and it's got fully independent suspension.

9
00:02:01,345 --> 00:02:03,714
It's a three-speed, dual-motor system.

10
00:02:04,181 --> 00:02:07,584
I spent 100,000 yen modding it. It's my pride and joy!

11
00:02:09,152 --> 00:02:12,656
The car's pretty cool, but my driving skills are even better.

12
00:02:12,956 --> 00:02:14,358
Awesome!

13
00:02:14,791 --> 00:02:16,660
Ryo-san, you're great at this!

14
00:02:18,028 --> 00:02:19,463
-So cool! -What's going on?

15
00:02:19,963 --> 00:02:22,332
Check out this next trick.

16
00:02:22,966 --> 00:02:25,269
Go! Super jump!

17
00:02:26,370 --> 00:02:27,638
Excuse me.

18
00:02:34,144 --> 00:02:36,113
What'd you go and do that for, Chief?

19
00:02:36,313 --> 00:02:38,615
You just appeared out of nowhere.

20
00:02:39,449 --> 00:02:40,918
Is the BUGATTI okay?

21
00:02:41,118 --> 00:02:42,586
It's not damaged at all!

22
00:02:42,920 --> 00:02:47,057
It's got a reinforced frame. It won't break just from hitting someone.

23
00:02:47,624 --> 00:02:48,759
Ryotsu...

24
00:02:49,359 --> 00:02:51,495
Yes! What is it, Chief?

25
00:02:52,162 --> 00:02:53,697
Where are we?

26
00:02:54,064 --> 00:02:57,534
Come on, Chief. You're not old enough to be senile yet.

27
00:02:57,768 --> 00:03:00,204
We're obviously at the police station.

28
00:03:00,704 --> 00:03:04,975
Did that whack to the nuts make you lose your memory?

29
00:03:05,509 --> 00:03:07,844
It's me, Ryotsu!

30
00:03:08,045 --> 00:03:10,681
Do you understand...?

31
00:03:12,182 --> 00:03:15,152
You moron!

32
00:03:15,619 --> 00:03:18,155
Ryotsu! Do you know what a police station is?

33
00:03:18,355 --> 00:03:20,157
Is it a kids' playground?

34
00:03:20,357 --> 00:03:21,858
Is it a track for RC cars?

35
00:03:22,359 --> 00:03:26,263
It is not! It's the sacred workplace of us police officers!

36
00:03:26,730 --> 00:03:31,034
You don't have to shout so loud, Chief. I can hear what you're saying.

37
00:03:31,234 --> 00:03:33,270
You're not suffering from amnesia.

38
00:03:33,503 --> 00:03:35,272
That's not what I'm saying!

39
00:03:35,806 --> 00:03:38,508
I have had it up to here with you!

40
00:03:39,109 --> 00:03:40,077
As of right now,

41
00:03:40,277 --> 00:03:44,581
all personal belongings unrelated to work are strictly prohibited!

42
00:03:45,115 --> 00:03:47,050
That's an order!

43
00:03:47,250 --> 00:03:48,919
What?!

44
00:03:49,820 --> 00:03:52,256
"RYOTSU MAY NOT BRING PERSONAL ITEMS TO WORK"

45
00:03:55,826 --> 00:03:57,294
Appalling.

46
00:03:57,527 --> 00:03:59,930
Just look at all these personal items.

47
00:04:00,297 --> 00:04:04,034
There's still more to go. We couldn't fit them all on one bike.

48
00:04:05,068 --> 00:04:07,037
That'll need another three trips.

49
00:04:08,205 --> 00:04:11,742
Listen up. Once you're done unloading, come straight back here.

50
00:04:12,075 --> 00:04:13,377
Yeah, yeah.

51
00:04:17,481 --> 00:04:22,019
That man can't tell the difference between a workplace and a playground.

52
00:04:23,854 --> 00:04:26,857
This is it. The car that hit me earlier.

53
00:04:27,591 --> 00:04:29,626
I'd love to rip it apart.

54
00:04:30,093 --> 00:04:32,429
That cost 100,000 yen, apparently.

55
00:04:32,629 --> 00:04:35,599
What? 100,000 yen for a toy?

56
00:04:37,267 --> 00:04:40,437
I can't believe someone would spend so much on this.

57
00:04:42,039 --> 00:04:43,640
What's this?

58
00:04:44,808 --> 00:04:45,942
A radio?

59
00:04:48,478 --> 00:04:49,646
I can't hear anything.

60
00:04:50,447 --> 00:04:51,815
How do you turn it on?

61
00:04:56,253 --> 00:04:59,423
Terai, did it really cost 100,000 yen?

62
00:04:59,623 --> 00:05:01,358
Yes, I think so...

63
00:05:01,792 --> 00:05:02,993
This is bad.

64
00:05:04,361 --> 00:05:06,163
It's in the middle of the road.

65
00:05:06,997 --> 00:05:10,100
Hurry up and stop it before any cars come!

66
00:05:10,534 --> 00:05:12,102
How do you stop it?

67
00:05:13,603 --> 00:05:14,805
It's going faster!

68
00:05:15,439 --> 00:05:17,340
Terai, you do it.

69
00:05:17,541 --> 00:05:18,942
I don't know how.

70
00:05:19,142 --> 00:05:20,777
Oh, a car's coming!

71
00:05:22,446 --> 00:05:23,313
Oh no!

72
00:05:26,283 --> 00:05:27,684
No, don't stop there!

73
00:05:33,190 --> 00:05:34,791
That was close.

74
00:05:34,991 --> 00:05:36,927
Another car's coming.

75
00:05:37,794 --> 00:05:39,496
Oh no! Not that way!

76
00:05:40,764 --> 00:05:42,632
I'm inching closer to death here.

77
00:05:46,570 --> 00:05:48,372
I think I'm starting to get it.

78
00:05:49,473 --> 00:05:51,875
There's a dump truck coming from the right!

79
00:05:52,109 --> 00:05:54,311
Okay, I'll move it to the other lane.

80
00:05:56,146 --> 00:05:58,248
-Nice! -We're safe now.

81
00:06:03,220 --> 00:06:04,421
It didn't hit it!

82
00:06:04,654 --> 00:06:06,256
That gave me a fright.

83
00:06:06,790 --> 00:06:08,792
All right, let's get it while we can.

84
00:06:08,992 --> 00:06:10,227
Okay! Oh!

85
00:06:18,502 --> 00:06:20,537
It might survive hitting someone,

86
00:06:20,737 --> 00:06:24,274
but it's no match for a steamroller.

87
00:06:25,275 --> 00:06:26,910
What do we do?

88
00:06:27,144 --> 00:06:29,679
He'll be furious.

89
00:06:30,013 --> 00:06:30,881
Hmm...

90
00:06:36,853 --> 00:06:38,588
That was unusually fast.

91
00:06:39,089 --> 00:06:41,691
You told me to come straight back here.

92
00:06:41,892 --> 00:06:43,260
And there's more to go.

93
00:06:43,460 --> 00:06:45,228
Th-That's right.

94
00:06:45,428 --> 00:06:48,999
I must be getting forgetful in my old age.

95
00:06:49,199 --> 00:06:52,702
Huh? Where did the BUGATTI go?

96
00:06:52,903 --> 00:06:56,640
Chief, have you seen my BUGATTI?

97
00:06:56,873 --> 00:06:59,643
It's the RC car that hit you.

98
00:07:00,010 --> 00:07:00,911
N-No...

99
00:07:01,111 --> 00:07:03,280
I thought I left it here.

100
00:07:03,480 --> 00:07:07,584
Oh, those kids from earlier came and borrowed it.

101
00:07:08,285 --> 00:07:09,319
Yes, that's right.

102
00:07:09,653 --> 00:07:11,888
What? You lent it to them without asking?

103
00:07:12,088 --> 00:07:13,089
Oh, uh...

104
00:07:13,657 --> 00:07:15,225
Hmm? This is odd.

105
00:07:15,425 --> 00:07:18,495
I saw Junpei and the others on the way back here.

106
00:07:19,629 --> 00:07:23,333
Oh, well, maybe it was some other kids.

107
00:07:23,567 --> 00:07:26,603
You do know a lot of kids, after all.

108
00:07:26,803 --> 00:07:27,504
Chief...

109
00:07:28,572 --> 00:07:31,341
Did you really lend it to the kids?

110
00:07:31,875 --> 00:07:33,243
Yes. I'm telling you.

111
00:07:33,443 --> 00:07:35,111
I wouldn't tell a lie.

112
00:07:36,746 --> 00:07:38,315
Are you sure?

113
00:07:39,316 --> 00:07:42,085
I'm not... lying.

114
00:07:42,285 --> 00:07:43,954
Why are you looking away?

115
00:07:44,154 --> 00:07:47,891
If you're not lying, you should be able to look me straight in the eye.

116
00:07:48,325 --> 00:07:50,627
Of course I can look you in the eye.

117
00:07:54,664 --> 00:07:57,100
&lt;i&gt;Damn it. If I look away, I lose.&lt;/i&gt;

118
00:08:04,841 --> 00:08:07,177
I knew it! You're hiding something!

119
00:08:07,978 --> 00:08:11,648
Huh? Why is the remote control here?

120
00:08:12,115 --> 00:08:12,916
Ah!

121
00:08:14,484 --> 00:08:17,020
Th-This can't be...

122
00:08:17,687 --> 00:08:20,790
My BUGATTI Ryotsu Special!

123
00:08:21,124 --> 00:08:25,729
Chief Ohara accidentally started it, and it got run over by a steamroller.

124
00:08:25,962 --> 00:08:26,796
You tattletale.

125
00:08:27,197 --> 00:08:29,132
Chief!

126
00:08:30,133 --> 00:08:32,802
This is your fault, if you think about it.

127
00:08:33,003 --> 00:08:34,738
If you hadn't brought it here...

128
00:08:34,971 --> 00:08:37,874
You broke my property and now you're blaming me?

129
00:08:38,575 --> 00:08:40,343
I'm the victim here!

130
00:08:40,544 --> 00:08:42,112
You hit me in the groin!

131
00:08:42,312 --> 00:08:45,382
And that makes it okay to destroy my pride and joy?

132
00:08:46,182 --> 00:08:49,219
I'm sorry that it happened.

133
00:08:49,719 --> 00:08:53,957
But ultimately, it was your bad behavior that led to this outcome.

134
00:08:54,157 --> 00:08:55,325
This was a warning.

135
00:08:55,725 --> 00:08:58,194
How dare you say it like that!

136
00:08:58,395 --> 00:09:01,731
You could lick my boots, crying, and I'd never forgive you!

137
00:09:02,232 --> 00:09:06,736
If I have to lick your boots, I don't want your forgiveness.

138
00:09:08,171 --> 00:09:10,774
Come on, both of you. We're all adults here.

139
00:09:11,007 --> 00:09:12,876
-Shut up! -Shut up!

140
00:09:14,511 --> 00:09:16,413
Take this! And this!

141
00:09:18,081 --> 00:09:19,616
So that's what happened, huh?

142
00:09:19,983 --> 00:09:20,917
Why you...!

143
00:09:21,151 --> 00:09:23,253
Hey, don't collapse on me yet.

144
00:09:23,453 --> 00:09:26,856
I'll show him for what he did to me today.

145
00:09:27,590 --> 00:09:28,758
Poor Chief Ohara.

146
00:09:29,726 --> 00:09:34,764
Oh, speaking of, I wanted to show you the chief in the station newsletter.

147
00:09:35,398 --> 00:09:36,933
What? That rotten chief?

148
00:09:37,334 --> 00:09:40,270
He's in the "My Pride And Joy" section.

149
00:09:40,804 --> 00:09:41,805
What's that?

150
00:09:42,038 --> 00:09:45,909
"Chief Ohara of Kameari Park Police Station's pride and joy

151
00:09:46,109 --> 00:09:49,212
is his newly renovated cypress wood bath.

152
00:09:49,412 --> 00:09:53,350
'A cypress bath at the end of the day makes all my fatigue disappear.

153
00:09:53,750 --> 00:09:56,753
It's like being in heaven.'"

154
00:09:56,953 --> 00:09:57,821
How dare you!

155
00:09:58,722 --> 00:10:02,392
You ruin my pride and joy, and you're bragging about your own?

156
00:10:04,361 --> 00:10:08,431
Serves you right for being a show-off with your bath.

157
00:10:08,632 --> 00:10:10,133
Hmm? Wait a minute...

158
00:10:10,900 --> 00:10:12,602
If he treasures his bath...

159
00:10:15,505 --> 00:10:18,575
Is this what you meant by a bath salt set?

160
00:10:19,242 --> 00:10:22,312
Why did you send me out to buy this?

161
00:10:22,779 --> 00:10:25,315
It's a gift for the chief.

162
00:10:25,515 --> 00:10:27,150
But...

163
00:10:28,518 --> 00:10:30,320
I'm switching out the contents.

164
00:10:31,254 --> 00:10:33,490
They'll be extra-special bath salts.

165
00:10:33,690 --> 00:10:36,626
Ground chili peppers, wasabi powder, and pepper.

166
00:10:36,826 --> 00:10:38,828
It'll do wonders for the circulation.

167
00:10:40,063 --> 00:10:41,331
Honda. Try some.

168
00:10:41,531 --> 00:10:43,133
What? Me?

169
00:10:43,500 --> 00:10:46,269
Just a spoonful. Quit your whining.

170
00:10:46,469 --> 00:10:47,670
But...

171
00:10:47,871 --> 00:10:48,772
Here!

172
00:10:55,445 --> 00:10:58,548
He'll die of shock if he puts this in his bath.

173
00:10:58,782 --> 00:11:01,017
That's a bit dramatic. It's not—

174
00:11:03,653 --> 00:11:05,522
Wow, it might actually kill him.

175
00:11:06,790 --> 00:11:08,692
Powdered milk will make it mild.

176
00:11:09,192 --> 00:11:11,728
Into the "Famous Hot Spring Village" packet...

177
00:11:12,162 --> 00:11:14,798
and seal it tight, just like before.

178
00:11:15,432 --> 00:11:17,901
Done! The first special bath salt is ready.

179
00:11:18,134 --> 00:11:20,303
I call it "Extra-Hot Spring"!

180
00:11:21,004 --> 00:11:24,307
It's a shame I won't get to watch the chief panic.

181
00:11:27,577 --> 00:11:28,712
Next, the second one.

182
00:11:28,912 --> 00:11:31,214
Mouse droppings and sparrow droppings,

183
00:11:31,714 --> 00:11:35,585
with a touch of chicken and goldfish poop as well.

184
00:11:35,819 --> 00:11:37,587
Where did you even get all that?

185
00:11:37,821 --> 00:11:40,757
"Forest Fragrance" becomes "Manure Fragrance."

186
00:11:40,990 --> 00:11:42,125
That's intense.

187
00:11:43,193 --> 00:11:45,762
Next, miso, tea-soaked rice, and consommé soup.

188
00:11:45,995 --> 00:11:48,465
We'll get a great broth from the chief with this.

189
00:11:49,332 --> 00:11:51,734
What shall I mix next?

190
00:11:51,935 --> 00:11:52,836
I know...

191
00:11:53,036 --> 00:11:55,572
Musk, ginseng extract, and a fur seal's...

192
00:11:55,772 --> 00:11:58,141
This is getting fun!

193
00:11:58,341 --> 00:12:00,477
And I'm getting scared.

194
00:12:01,010 --> 00:12:04,013
Finally, the ultimate special bath salt.

195
00:12:04,481 --> 00:12:08,751
This plaster is a special formula that hardens quickly.

196
00:12:09,319 --> 00:12:11,755
By the time he notices, it'll be rock-hard!

197
00:12:13,223 --> 00:12:15,325
We'll have a mold of the chief.

198
00:12:15,525 --> 00:12:17,427
We could make a 1:1 scale doll.

199
00:12:18,094 --> 00:12:20,730
What a great gift this turned out to be.

200
00:12:21,531 --> 00:12:24,434
I'll send it to the chief's house by courier.

201
00:12:24,767 --> 00:12:27,871
But he'll be suspicious if it's from me.

202
00:12:28,238 --> 00:12:30,640
I'll send it under the superintendent's name.

203
00:12:30,874 --> 00:12:32,108
He's so cunning...

204
00:12:32,709 --> 00:12:35,712
Relax and enjoy your gift, Chief.

205
00:12:35,912 --> 00:12:39,082
It'll be a bath you'll never forget.

206
00:12:52,962 --> 00:12:55,064
"OZAKI MODEL SHOP"

207
00:12:59,569 --> 00:13:01,070
Chief Ohara.

208
00:13:01,905 --> 00:13:03,473
Reiko and Nakagawa?

209
00:13:03,973 --> 00:13:08,645
You still feel bad about having broken Ryo-chan's remote-controlled car?

210
00:13:11,014 --> 00:13:15,652
Regardless of the reason, the fact is that I broke something that cost 100,000 yen.

211
00:13:16,386 --> 00:13:18,855
Ryotsu hasn't spoken to me since.

212
00:13:19,088 --> 00:13:22,125
I feel I've lost my chance to make it up to him.

213
00:13:22,325 --> 00:13:24,294
What a mess.

214
00:13:24,694 --> 00:13:26,296
Hey, I have an idea.

215
00:13:30,166 --> 00:13:32,702
What? You're going to treat me to dinner?

216
00:13:32,936 --> 00:13:34,871
You and Nakagawa?

217
00:13:35,104 --> 00:13:38,241
Yes. We wanted to thank you for everything you do for us.

218
00:13:38,775 --> 00:13:41,978
Well, how nice of you. What are you going to treat me to?

219
00:13:42,478 --> 00:13:44,848
That's a surprise for you to find out.

220
00:13:45,048 --> 00:13:47,483
Kei-chan should be here soon to pick us up.

221
00:13:47,850 --> 00:13:50,854
Then buckle me in and take me anywhere!

222
00:13:51,054 --> 00:13:55,959
&lt;i&gt;And the chief should be getting&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;a special bath salt delivery today.&lt;/i&gt;

223
00:13:56,159 --> 00:13:59,495
-&lt;i&gt;This is the best day ever!&lt;/i&gt; -Ryo-chan, he's here.

224
00:13:59,896 --> 00:14:01,164
Thanks for waiting.

225
00:14:01,364 --> 00:14:02,999
Hey, thanks for coming.

226
00:14:03,466 --> 00:14:06,636
Wow, a limousine to pick us up? That's pretty fancy.

227
00:14:07,136 --> 00:14:10,273
It's got alcohol, a TV, karaoke, and games too.

228
00:14:10,473 --> 00:14:11,474
Let me see.

229
00:14:12,508 --> 00:14:14,010
Would you look at this!

230
00:14:16,512 --> 00:14:19,716
I'm even more excited for dinner now.

231
00:14:22,919 --> 00:14:24,354
We're here.

232
00:14:28,925 --> 00:14:32,161
I wonder what we'll be eating.

233
00:14:32,362 --> 00:14:33,062
Huh?

234
00:14:34,397 --> 00:14:37,200
I don't see any fancy restaurants.

235
00:14:37,400 --> 00:14:39,769
Wait, isn't this...

236
00:14:40,670 --> 00:14:42,238
It's the chief's house!

237
00:14:42,739 --> 00:14:46,542
Chief Ohara wants to make up with you, so...

238
00:14:46,743 --> 00:14:47,477
Hey!

239
00:14:47,677 --> 00:14:48,945
Take me home, Nakagawa.

240
00:14:49,479 --> 00:14:50,580
Wait, Ryo-chan.

241
00:14:52,181 --> 00:14:55,518
I don't like that you're trying to win me over with food.

242
00:14:56,019 --> 00:14:58,388
That's 100,000 yen I lost there!

243
00:14:58,588 --> 00:15:01,891
But the chief's already prepared a feast for us.

244
00:15:02,492 --> 00:15:04,661
He'd never make anything special.

245
00:15:05,261 --> 00:15:07,363
Probably sashimi and tonkatsu at best.

246
00:15:07,563 --> 00:15:09,799
His generation are all penny-pinchers.

247
00:15:10,033 --> 00:15:10,667
Huh?

248
00:15:11,367 --> 00:15:14,103
Excuse me for being a penny-pincher.

249
00:15:15,338 --> 00:15:16,906
Thanks for coming out.

250
00:15:17,106 --> 00:15:18,041
Chief...

251
00:15:18,241 --> 00:15:20,710
You almost gave me a heart attack.

252
00:15:22,145 --> 00:15:23,246
Ryotsu.

253
00:15:24,213 --> 00:15:27,250
I... I must say, the other day...

254
00:15:27,450 --> 00:15:28,751
I have to say...

255
00:15:30,219 --> 00:15:32,455
I saw a smart-looking sumo wrestler!

256
00:15:32,689 --> 00:15:33,289
What?

257
00:15:34,057 --> 00:15:37,794
Anyway, let's not stand around. Please, come inside.

258
00:15:38,361 --> 00:15:40,363
-Yes. -Let's do that.

259
00:15:40,563 --> 00:15:42,098
Isn't he going to apologize?

260
00:15:42,298 --> 00:15:43,933
He's embarrassed.

261
00:15:44,400 --> 00:15:45,802
Is Hiromi-san not here?

262
00:15:46,002 --> 00:15:48,104
She's on a ski trip with her friends.

263
00:15:48,304 --> 00:15:50,139
Now I really want to go home.

264
00:15:52,608 --> 00:15:54,711
Just as I expected.

265
00:15:55,278 --> 00:15:58,448
Go on. Eat as much as you like.

266
00:15:58,648 --> 00:16:00,616
You like sashimi and tonkatsu, right?

267
00:16:00,817 --> 00:16:03,152
I've prepared plenty, Ryotsu.

268
00:16:05,621 --> 00:16:07,857
This sashimi was frozen, wasn't it?

269
00:16:08,091 --> 00:16:12,462
You bought it on sale three days ago and kept it in the freezer, didn't you?

270
00:16:15,298 --> 00:16:18,568
And this tonkatsu is the cheap, sinewy stuff.

271
00:16:19,202 --> 00:16:22,038
And everything else is on the cheap too.

272
00:16:22,605 --> 00:16:26,509
This would all amount to around 850 yen per person, even with the sake.

273
00:16:26,743 --> 00:16:27,877
&lt;i&gt;He's sharp.&lt;/i&gt;

274
00:16:28,578 --> 00:16:33,983
850 yen for 100,000 yen of damage is quite the bargain. Isn't it, Chief?

275
00:16:34,784 --> 00:16:38,855
This meal is not a monetary substitute for the remote-controlled car.

276
00:16:40,323 --> 00:16:43,993
I plan to compensate you properly when I receive my bonus.

277
00:16:44,360 --> 00:16:46,696
Huh? You will?

278
00:16:47,363 --> 00:16:49,132
This is just a symbolic gesture.

279
00:16:49,332 --> 00:16:53,436
It's my way of apologizing. By inviting you to dinner.

280
00:16:53,636 --> 00:16:56,873
Then why didn't you say so, Chief?

281
00:16:57,073 --> 00:16:58,775
You old rascal!

282
00:16:58,975 --> 00:17:02,445
Oh, now that I have a closer look, it all looks delicious.

283
00:17:03,513 --> 00:17:05,815
My tonkatsu...

284
00:17:06,482 --> 00:17:11,687
The ingredients may be cheap, but if it's cooked well, it tastes good.

285
00:17:13,489 --> 00:17:16,092
Hey, don't eat mine. Eat your own.

286
00:17:16,626 --> 00:17:18,661
At least they've made up now.

287
00:17:18,861 --> 00:17:19,495
Yeah.

288
00:17:20,830 --> 00:17:22,632
Cheers!

289
00:17:25,468 --> 00:17:29,338
Say, Chief. Didn't you recently upgrade your bath to a cypress one?

290
00:17:29,539 --> 00:17:30,740
Can I see it?

291
00:17:31,107 --> 00:17:35,044
Sure, go ahead. We can use it 24/7.

292
00:17:35,478 --> 00:17:36,913
Would you like a bath?

293
00:17:37,113 --> 00:17:38,748
Thank you, I would.

294
00:17:39,248 --> 00:17:40,483
Top you off, Chief?

295
00:17:40,683 --> 00:17:41,751
Oh, thank you.

296
00:17:41,951 --> 00:17:44,654
A bath? How nice.

297
00:17:44,854 --> 00:17:46,522
Huh? A bath...?

298
00:17:47,290 --> 00:17:48,024
Oh!

299
00:17:48,591 --> 00:17:49,692
Chief!

300
00:17:50,593 --> 00:17:55,031
Do you use bath salts or anything like that?

301
00:17:55,231 --> 00:17:57,934
Normally, yes. But we ran out recently.

302
00:17:58,434 --> 00:18:02,105
Oh, really? That's too bad.

303
00:18:02,305 --> 00:18:06,108
&lt;i&gt;Guess my special bath salts&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;haven't arrived yet.&lt;/i&gt;

304
00:18:06,309 --> 00:18:08,845
You should have a bath later too.

305
00:18:09,045 --> 00:18:11,047
Yes! Thank you!

306
00:18:16,752 --> 00:18:17,787
This feels nice.

307
00:18:18,554 --> 00:18:20,923
Yeah, tonight's been fun.

308
00:18:21,124 --> 00:18:23,159
I haven't had this much fun in ages!

309
00:18:23,392 --> 00:18:24,327
You said it.

310
00:18:25,094 --> 00:18:29,632
Ryotsu, I feel so bad for what I did to your car.

311
00:18:29,866 --> 00:18:31,534
I hope you'll forgive me.

312
00:18:31,734 --> 00:18:33,336
It's fine.

313
00:18:33,569 --> 00:18:37,640
We'll take a bath together and wash the whole ordeal away in the hot water.

314
00:18:37,874 --> 00:18:40,710
All right. I'll wash your back for you.

315
00:18:42,879 --> 00:18:44,614
I had a really wonderful bath.

316
00:18:45,014 --> 00:18:46,015
Glad to hear it.

317
00:18:46,249 --> 00:18:48,284
Okay, it's our turn.

318
00:18:48,484 --> 00:18:50,319
I'm looking forward to it.

319
00:18:50,753 --> 00:18:53,890
Reiko, you can join us too, if you want.

320
00:18:54,090 --> 00:18:55,625
I wouldn't say no to that!

321
00:18:56,125 --> 00:18:58,494
The chief's gotten pretty drunk.

322
00:19:00,196 --> 00:19:01,497
Who is it at this hour?

323
00:19:01,731 --> 00:19:03,633
Ryotsu, you go on ahead and get in.

324
00:19:03,833 --> 00:19:04,734
Sure.

325
00:19:04,934 --> 00:19:06,169
Coming!

326
00:19:08,738 --> 00:19:12,909
Wow, that's a nice bath, given how stingy the chief usually is.

327
00:19:13,209 --> 00:19:14,810
Ah, the water is just right.

328
00:19:15,011 --> 00:19:16,379
-Hey, Ryotsu! -Huh?

329
00:19:17,013 --> 00:19:21,184
The superintendent sent me some bath salts by courier.

330
00:19:25,321 --> 00:19:27,356
&lt;i&gt;My special bath salts...&lt;/i&gt;

331
00:19:27,590 --> 00:19:29,859
What great timing. Let's use them now.

332
00:19:30,626 --> 00:19:31,594
Going somewhere?

333
00:19:31,794 --> 00:19:35,064
I just remembered something urgent...

334
00:19:35,531 --> 00:19:37,466
Surely you have time to take a bath!

335
00:19:37,667 --> 00:19:41,137
Actually, I'm allergic to cypress baths.

336
00:19:42,371 --> 00:19:44,006
Nice joke, Ryotsu.

337
00:19:44,206 --> 00:19:48,678
Actually, my late father's last wish was that I never take a cypress bath.

338
00:19:48,878 --> 00:19:51,614
I know your father is alive and well.

339
00:19:51,814 --> 00:19:53,783
You said we'd take a bath together.

340
00:19:53,983 --> 00:19:55,384
No, wait...!

341
00:19:56,219 --> 00:19:58,554
There are so many. It's hard to choose.

342
00:19:59,522 --> 00:20:02,992
All right, let's go with this one. "Forest Fragrance."

343
00:20:03,192 --> 00:20:04,260
&lt;i&gt;"Manure Fragrance."&lt;/i&gt;

344
00:20:07,029 --> 00:20:08,798
Stir it well...

345
00:20:09,632 --> 00:20:11,267
Ugh, it stinks!

346
00:20:11,801 --> 00:20:13,970
Ah, that's a nice scent.

347
00:20:14,704 --> 00:20:17,240
&lt;i&gt;He's so drunk he hasn't even noticed.&lt;/i&gt;

348
00:20:17,974 --> 00:20:20,910
Ryotsu, how good are cypress baths?

349
00:20:21,110 --> 00:20:24,747
Yeah, you're right. Cypress baths are the best.

350
00:20:24,981 --> 00:20:28,184
Ah, that's nice. I feel so refreshed.

351
00:20:28,384 --> 00:20:29,885
Okay, I'll leave you to it.

352
00:20:30,086 --> 00:20:33,289
Hey! You didn't even get in the tub!

353
00:20:34,724 --> 00:20:36,592
Stop it, Chief!

354
00:20:36,993 --> 00:20:38,594
Men shouldn't bear hug naked!

355
00:20:39,362 --> 00:20:43,933
Ryotsu... You said we'd take a bath together and wash the whole ordeal away.

356
00:20:45,768 --> 00:20:47,069
Okay.

357
00:20:47,269 --> 00:20:49,105
You just want me in the tub, yeah?

358
00:20:49,872 --> 00:20:52,074
Up to your neck, you hear?

359
00:20:52,608 --> 00:20:54,410
Why me?

360
00:20:54,910 --> 00:20:56,445
Let's put another one in.

361
00:20:57,680 --> 00:20:58,781
"Extra-Hot Spring!"

362
00:20:59,248 --> 00:21:00,750
No, not that one! You—

363
00:21:00,950 --> 00:21:02,718
Up to your neck, remember?

364
00:21:05,554 --> 00:21:06,722
What's wrong?

365
00:21:07,156 --> 00:21:11,327
My mucous membranes... Um, I mean, my hemorrhoids have been acting up lately.

366
00:21:11,560 --> 00:21:15,398
&lt;i&gt;My whole body is on fire.&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;I thought I was gonna die from shock.&lt;/i&gt;

367
00:21:16,599 --> 00:21:17,566
Thank you.

368
00:21:17,900 --> 00:21:20,603
Oh, it's no trouble at all.

369
00:21:21,037 --> 00:21:22,304
&lt;i&gt;Better dilute it quick.&lt;/i&gt;

370
00:21:22,738 --> 00:21:25,241
Okay, now I'll wash your back.

371
00:21:25,441 --> 00:21:26,942
Oh no, that's okay.

372
00:21:27,343 --> 00:21:29,245
You won't let me wash your back?

373
00:21:29,445 --> 00:21:32,248
O-Of course you can. Please, go ahead.

374
00:21:32,782 --> 00:21:35,785
-All right. I'm a good back washer. -Sure you are.

375
00:21:38,587 --> 00:21:42,892
No matter how dirty it is, all I need is one scrub!

376
00:21:46,829 --> 00:21:49,932
Chief! That's a wire scrubber!

377
00:21:50,132 --> 00:21:51,534
Oops, my mistake.

378
00:21:52,335 --> 00:21:55,338
Your back is so rough, I mistook it for a tile.

379
00:21:55,538 --> 00:21:57,339
How is that possible?

380
00:22:01,844 --> 00:22:03,279
It stings!

381
00:22:04,213 --> 00:22:06,215
Oh, this is tile cleaner.

382
00:22:06,449 --> 00:22:07,550
-I'm out! -Wait!

383
00:22:10,186 --> 00:22:11,787
We've not bathed together yet.

384
00:22:11,987 --> 00:22:15,357
I told you not to bear hug me while naked! It's disgusting!

385
00:22:15,558 --> 00:22:17,693
Then get in the tub with me, Ryotsu.

386
00:22:17,927 --> 00:22:21,831
Let's have some male bonding time.

387
00:22:23,299 --> 00:22:24,467
&lt;i&gt;This is hell...&lt;/i&gt;

388
00:22:25,134 --> 00:22:30,306
Chief, isn't it a waste to be so close in such a big bath? We could move apart?

389
00:22:30,706 --> 00:22:31,774
Yeah, you're right.

390
00:22:33,642 --> 00:22:36,479
Let's add a little more bath salt.

391
00:22:39,782 --> 00:22:41,517
No, not that one!

392
00:22:43,385 --> 00:22:45,054
Oh no!

393
00:22:45,421 --> 00:22:47,556
We have to get out quickly!

394
00:22:50,259 --> 00:22:54,597
You just got in! Do you really hate being in the bath with me that much?

395
00:22:55,398 --> 00:22:58,367
No, it's not that! We have to get out now or else!

396
00:22:58,567 --> 00:22:59,735
Or else what?

397
00:22:59,969 --> 00:23:02,037
You just poured plaster into the bath.

398
00:23:02,238 --> 00:23:04,807
Why would there be plaster in bath salt?

399
00:23:05,908 --> 00:23:09,211
Hmm? Feels like my body's getting heavier.

400
00:23:09,411 --> 00:23:11,046
It's starting to harden.

401
00:23:11,514 --> 00:23:14,183
Like I said, it's plaster. We need to get out now!

402
00:23:14,383 --> 00:23:15,518
-Hold it! -Huh?

403
00:23:16,619 --> 00:23:19,822
How did you know the bath salt was plaster?

404
00:23:20,222 --> 00:23:24,560
You're up to something again, aren't you?

405
00:23:24,760 --> 00:23:27,029
Never mind that. Let's get out of here!

406
00:23:27,229 --> 00:23:28,531
What was that shouting?

407
00:23:28,731 --> 00:23:30,733
It sounded like Ryo-chan's voice.

408
00:23:30,933 --> 00:23:32,735
Somebody help us!

409
00:23:32,935 --> 00:23:33,736
The bathroom!

410
00:23:36,372 --> 00:23:38,107
Nakagawa! Help us!

411
00:23:38,307 --> 00:23:39,942
I can't move!

412
00:23:40,476 --> 00:23:43,712
What were you thinking when you made this thing? You moron!

413
00:23:44,180 --> 00:23:47,850
It's all your fault for breaking my remote-controlled car!

414
00:23:48,050 --> 00:23:50,085
Are you still going on about that?

415
00:23:50,619 --> 00:23:51,754
Ouch!

416
00:23:51,954 --> 00:23:55,057
It seems they're back to square one.

417
00:23:55,257 --> 00:23:56,859
They're hopeless.

418
00:23:59,128 --> 00:24:00,963
Do something!

419
00:24:01,197 --> 00:24:03,199
It's getting harder!
